47:04.364 --> 47:08.206
And I'm just looking at this really quick

47:08.706 --> 47:19.388
to make sure that we— it

47:19.888 --> 47:22.956
says here water for the residential use shall be required

47:23.456 --> 47:27.170
through the master development plan and agreement application process. As we—

47:27.299 --> 47:30.422
I think as we talked, and maybe Marcus, you might remember this, but I felt

47:30.471 --> 47:34.726
like we had talked about the idea of that water

47:35.226 --> 47:39.127
being nailed down by no later than the master

47:39.143 --> 47:42.515
development agreement. It would be done by at

47:43.015 --> 47:46.530
least that time. Yeah, kind of the discussion is essentially that, you know,

47:47.574 --> 47:51.316
what we've encountered in our history as a city

47:52.006 --> 47:56.058
is that applicants will come in, They'll get vesting

47:56.639 --> 48:00.173
and have really no, like, and then just sell it and get out of them

48:00.528 --> 48:04.370
and get out, right? Because the biggest increase in the value of the property

48:04.790 --> 48:07.134
comes with the vesting. Yeah. So,

48:08.848 --> 48:12.420
what happens is there's no actual plan as to how to develop

48:12.920 --> 48:16.805
the property. There has, in a lot of cases historically, there was no actual plan

48:17.242 --> 48:20.703
on how to develop the property at the time that they got vesting. They're like,

48:20.719 --> 48:24.380
great. We have this vesting. It's going to get,

48:24.400 --> 48:27.660
you know, in the older history of the city, it was like we're

48:28.160 --> 48:31.340
going to be entitled to X number of units, and there's going to have the

48:31.840 --> 48:34.700
zoning. And so it's not totally without a plan. But how we're going to,

48:35.200 --> 48:37.430
you know, bring water to the property or any of the utilities,

48:38.480 --> 48:42.220
how, you know, we're going to, you know, dedicate the water, that's all just going

48:42.720 --> 48:46.720
to be figured out later. That's kind of been the approach. And what we

48:47.220 --> 48:50.588
have is a situation where we have, you know, 20,000 plus units that are

48:50.636 --> 48:53.173
vested, quote unquote, in our city,

48:53.751 --> 48:56.882
and the majority of them have no water associated

48:57.382 --> 49:00.768
with them and no way to develop. And it just creates a situation where

49:01.268 --> 49:04.301
you have these properties who are just sitting there that, you know,

49:05.714 --> 49:09.792
can't be developed realistically. And it just doesn't make any sense for anybody involved

49:09.808 --> 49:13.132
for a property to be vested. So the periods,

49:13.260 --> 49:16.857
you know, in a situation where someone is applying for a master development plan,

49:17.355 --> 49:21.369
then it's going to be at the time that the MDP is approved and

49:21.869 --> 49:26.154
then the subsequent master development agreement is approved and executed.

49:26.202 --> 49:30.553
That's when the vesting occurs. The master development plan approval is always contingent

49:31.083 --> 49:34.423
on the execution of the agreement. And if that agreement

49:34.923 --> 49:38.325
never gets executed, then the approval is void. So that's really the

49:38.825 --> 49:41.871
period where vesting occurs, when that master development agreement is approved and executed.

49:42.211 --> 49:45.596
So it makes sense that the water rights then be

49:46.096 --> 49:50.216
conveyed at that time when vesting occurs. On the flip

49:50.716 --> 49:52.906
side, you know, when there is no master development plan,

49:54.211 --> 49:57.642
would be typically a smaller development of less

49:57.675 --> 50:01.636
than 50 acres, or, you know, somebody applies for a master development plan waiver in

50:02.136 --> 50:04.180
accordance with our ordinance and it's granted,

50:05.403 --> 50:08.056
then it would be preliminary plat is basically when you're vesting,

50:09.445 --> 50:13.319
you know, the sort of density of the property, and that would be the time

50:13.819 --> 50:16.868
where it would make the most sense, at least certainly in a residential context,

50:17.366 --> 50:20.820
for delivering water rights so

50:21.320 --> 50:24.965
that, hey, we know this property can actually be developed, as opposed to we have

50:24.997 --> 50:28.131
this vesting and it's just going to sit there idle for, in some cases,

50:28.246 --> 50:29.307
you know, decades. All right.

50:32.860 --> 50:36.551
